Subject: [PATCH] adwaita decoration: read portal settings before the first paint

loadConfiguration() ran from a zero-delay timer and read the
xdg-desktop-portal settings asynchronously, so a window was first painted
with the default light colors and button layout and then changed a moment
later. Call it from the constructor, load the icons and default colors
first, and query the portal synchronously with a 200 ms timeout, falling
back to the asynchronous call if the portal is slow. Move the reply
handling into applySettings(), and skip requestRepaint() while the
decoration has no window yet.

--- a/src/plugins/decorations/adwaita/qwaylandadwaitadecoration.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/decorations/adwaita/qwaylandadwaitadecoration.cpp
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@
 #include <QtDBus/QDBusPendingCall>
 #include <QtDBus/QDBusPendingCallWatcher>
